    "historyMessages": 1,
    "response": "# Skill: Validate and Activate a JSON Query Observation Extractor\n\n## Objective\nCreate, validate, activate, and use a JavaScript observation processor for `json_query` that extracts answer values across specified input formats.\n\n## Prerequisites\n- Access to `harness_inspect`\n- Access to `harness_propose`\n- Access to `harness_evaluate`\n- Access to `harness_activate`\n- Access to `json_query`\n- The processor source must be a JavaScript function body that receives `observation` with `{ toolName, text }` and returns a string.\n\n## Steps\n1. Call `harness_inspect` with an empty argument object to retrieve processor requirements, validation examples, and the active revision state.\n2. Write a JavaScript function body that:\n   - Reads `observation.text`.\n   - Attempts to parse text as JSON and returns the `answer` property when present.\n   - Detects CSV with an `answer` column and returns the answer value from the first data row.\n   - Detects key-value text in the form `answer=<value>`.\n   - Returns the original text unchanged for unknown formats.\n3. Propose the processor using `harness_propose`, specifying:\n   - `toolName: \"json_query\"`\n   - `baseRevision: null` when no active revision exists\n   - A revision label\n   - The source function body\n4. Record the revision ID returned by `harness_propose`.\n5. Call `harness_evaluate` with the returned revision ID.\n6. Confirm that evaluation reports `passed=true`.\n7. Call `harness_activate` with the validated revision ID.\n8. Read the activation observation; activation may be pending until the next tool step.\n9. Call `json_query` with an empty argument object to trigger the newly activated processor.\n10. Read the `json_query` observation and return only the extracted value.\n\n## Tools Used\n- `harness_inspect`\n- `harness_propose`\n- `harness_evaluate`\n- `harness_activate`\n- `json_query`\n\n## Notes\n- Reissue a tool call if the first invocation does not produce an observation.\n- Do not activate an unevaluated or failing revision.\n- Activation may take effect on the following tool call, so `json_query` should be called after receiving the activation response.\n- Preserve unknown or unstructured input exactly by returning `observation.text`.\n- Use `Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(o, \"answer\")` for JSON so falsy values such as `0`, `false`, or an empty string are still recognized.\n- A suitable processor body is:\n\n```javascript\nconst t = observation.text;\ntry {\n  const o = JSON.parse(t);\n  if (o && Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(o, \"answer\")) return String(o.answer);\n} catch (_) {}\n\nconst csv = t.match(/(?:^|\\n)\\s*[^,\\n]*,answer\\s*\\n\\s*[^,\\n]*,([^\\n\\r]*)/i);\nif (csv) return csv[1].trim();\n\nconst kv = t.match(/\\banswer\\s*=\\s*([^\\s,;]+)/i);\nif (kv) return kv[1];\n\nreturn t;\n```"
