    "historyMessages": 1,
    "response": "# Skill: Build and Validate a Format-Aware Observation Processor\n\n## Objective\nInspect a harness specification and create a JavaScript function-body processor that extracts answers from supported JSON, CSV, and `DATA answer=` formats while preserving unknown input unchanged.\n\n## Prerequisites\n- Access to the `harness_inspect` tool.\n- Target tool name, such as `json_query`.\n- Processor source must be a JavaScript function body that receives `observation` and returns a string.\n- No network, file-system, or asynchronous operations.\n\n## Steps\n1. Call `harness_inspect` for the target tool to read the supported input formats and processor constraints.\n2. Do not use a generic numeric regex extractor unless the harness explicitly requires number extraction; preserve the exact supported format semantics.\n3. Create a processor function body that:\n   - Reads `observation.text`.\n   - Attempts to parse the full text as JSON.\n   - If parsed JSON is an object with an own `answer` property, returns `String(obj.answer)`.\n   - Otherwise recognizes a single CSV record and returns the second field.\n   - Otherwise recognizes `DATA answer=<value>` and returns the captured value.\n   - Returns the original text unchanged for unsupported formats.\n4. Submit the source to `harness_inspect` with a revision name and the target `toolName`.\n5. Review the harness response to ensure the processor matches all listed formats and does not alter original tool status or provenance.\n6. After validation, activate the validated revision using the harness activation mechanism.\n7. Call `json_query` only after activation.\n8. Read the resulting observation after activation and return only the extracted answer required by the task.\n\nExample processor source:\n\n```js\nconst text = String(observation.text);\ntry {\n  const obj = JSON.parse(text);\n  if (obj && Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(obj, 'answer')) {\n    return String(obj.answer);\n  }\n} catch (_) {}\n\nconst csv = text.match(/^\\s*[^,\\r\\n]+\\s*,\\s*([^\\r\\n]+)\\s*$/);\nif (csv) return csv[1].trim();\n\nconst data = text.match(/^\\s*DATA\\s+answer\\s*=\\s*(.*?)\\s*$/i);\nif (data) return data[1];\n\nreturn text;\n```\n\n## Tools Used\n- `harness_inspect`\n- `json_query`\n\n## Notes\n- The required source is a function body, not a complete function declaration.\n- Use `Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(obj, 'answer')` so inherited properties are not treated as answers.\n- JSON parsing should be wrapped in `try/catch` so non-JSON formats continue to CSV and `DATA` checks.\n- The CSV matcher should target the expected two-column record and return the answer column, rather than assuming arbitrary numeric content.\n- Return unknown formats unchanged, as required by the harness.\n- The observed trajectory repeatedly inspected candidate source but did not show validation, activation, or a final `json_query` observation; a complete execution must perform those remaining steps."
